meta-rzg3l-fast-logo
====================

Seamless boot logo for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK: U-Boot brings the MIPI DSI ->
ADV7535 -> HDMI pipeline up and scans out a splash image, and the kernel
inherits that running pipeline instead of re-creating it, so the picture stays
on the screen from a few hundred milliseconds after reset until the compositor
draws its first frame.

Designed to be stacked on meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base, but it does not depend on
it: this layer is graphics only, that one is everything else.


I. What this layer changes
==========================

  U-Boot (recipes-bsp/u-boot/)
    0001  enable CONFIG_VIDEO for smarc-rzg3l
    0002  add drivers/video/rzg2l: CPG, DSI D-PHY, DSI link, ADV7535, DU and
          VSPD are programmed directly from init_sequence_r, before the main
          loop, and the splash is scanned out through a self-looping VSPD
          display list at 0x58000000
    0003  load the splash from /boot on the rootfs partition, and handle a
          failed load instead of scanning out uninitialised DRAM
    0004  wait for two output frames rather than a flat second

  Payload (recipes-graphics/rzg3l-boot-logo/)
    installs boot_img_720p.bin.gz and boot_img_1080p.bin.gz into /boot

  Kernel (recipes-kernel/linux/)
    0001  reserve 0x58000000..0x5fffffff no-map and move the CMA pool to
          0x70000000, so nothing overwrites the frame buffer or the display
          lists VSPD keeps fetching during boot
    0002  add "renesas,seamless-boot-logo" to vspd, du, dsi and the ADV7535
    0003  mark the MIPI DSI and LCDC module clocks CLK_IS_CRITICAL so
          clk_disable_unused() cannot gate the running pipeline
    0004  vsp1: take over the running pipeline instead of re-initialising it
    0005  rz-du: inherit a CRTC left running by the bootloader
    0006  rzg2l_mipi_dsi: inherit a link left streaming by the bootloader
    0007  adv7511: keep an HDMI output configured by the bootloader
    0008  adv7511: pin the connector to the bootloader's mode
    0009  adv7511: stop the ten second KMS connector poll from re-powering
          the encoder with an empty mode and taking the HDMI output down
    fast-logo.cfg  drop fbdev emulation, fbcon and the kernel logo, so the
          first DRM commit is the compositor's and not an all-black fbdev one


II. Required layers
===================

A standard RZ/G3L VLP project:

  poky/meta
  poky/meta-poky
  poky/meta-yocto-bsp
  meta-openembedded/meta-oe
  meta-openembedded/meta-python
  meta-openembedded/meta-multimedia
  meta-arm/meta-arm-toolchain
  meta-arm/meta-arm
  meta-renesas/meta-rz-bsp
  meta-renesas/meta-rz-distro
  meta-rz-features/meta-rz-codecs
  meta-rz-features/meta-rz-graphics
  meta-rzg3l-fast-logo

Tested with Yocto scarthgap, RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, u-boot 2024.07 and
linux-renesas 6.12.46-cip8, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l".


III. Build
==========

  $ source poky/oe-init-build-env build
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-fast-logo
  $ bitbake core-image-weston

No DISTRO setting is required - everything this layer does comes from bbappends
and one recipe, so it works with rz-vlp, with rz-vlp-fast from
meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base, or with any other distro.

conf/layer.conf adds rzg3l-boot-logo to IMAGE_INSTALL so that a plain
add-layer is enough. Set RZG3L_BOOT_LOGO_PACKAGE = "" in local.conf to build an
image without the payload.

Check that the pieces landed:

  $ strings tmp/deploy/images/smarc-rzg3l/fip.bin | grep boot_img
  ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48000000 boot/boot_img_720p.bin.gz

  $ fdtget tmp/deploy/images/smarc-rzg3l/r9a08g046l48-smarc.dtb \
        /soc/display@10890000 renesas,seamless-boot-logo


IV. Flashing
============

The splash is read by U-Boot, which lives inside fip.bin - NOT in the rootfs
image. Writing a new wic or rootfs does not update it. After every change to
this layer's U-Boot patches you must re-flash bl2 and fip to the boot medium
(Flash Writer over SCIF, or the eMMC boot-partition procedure in the RZ/G3L
Linux Start-up Guide).

The U-Boot version string is derived from SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, so an old and a
new build print exactly the same banner. Compare the size or timestamp of
fip.bin instead, or look for these lines on the console:

  62697 bytes read in ... ms
  Uncompressed size: 3686400 = 0x384000
  DU Init
  VCPD Init for DL


V. Changing the resolution
==========================

DISPLAY_MODE in drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c (patch 0002) selects both the
timings and which image file is loaded. It must stay in sync with the CEA VIC
pinned on the ADV7535 node by kernel patch 0008:

  MIPI_DSI_720P   ->  renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic = <4>
  MIPI_DSI_1080P  ->  renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic = <16>

If they disagree the kernel pins the connector to one mode while the hardware
scans out another.

The payload is a raw ARGB8888 frame buffer, gzip compressed. Its uncompressed
size must be exactly width * height * 4; the driver gunzips straight into the
reserved frame buffer and never checks the geometry. To ship your own artwork,
bbappend rzg3l-boot-logo from your own layer with FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend and
drop in files of the same names.


VI. Known limitations
=====================

  - The hand-over is declared statically in the device tree. If U-Boot does not
    actually leave the pipeline running - an old fip.bin, a different boot
    medium - the kernel still skips its own modeset and the display stays dark.
    Patch 0003 keeps the LCDC running even when the image fails to load, which
    covers the common case, but a runtime check in the kernel drivers, or
    having U-Boot add the DT property only on success, would be more robust.

  - Because kernel patch 0002 removes the ADV7535 interrupt and patch 0008
    drops DRM_BRIDGE_OP_HPD, drm_bridge_connector_init() puts the connector on
    the 10 second KMS poll. The poll itself is harmless since patch 0009, but
    it still runs; a connector that is pinned to one mode has nothing to poll
    for. Taking it off the poll would need either a way for the bridge to set
    connector->polled, or for rzg2l_du_encoder.c to clear it after
    drm_bridge_connector_init().

  - The BSP default environment has loadaddr=0x58000000, which is the splash
    frame buffer. Any manual "ext4load mmc 0:2 - <file>" or "tftp <file>" in
    U-Boot will overwrite the picture. Pass an explicit address.
